&lt;p&gt;Please join the Ukrainian Studies Program and the Harriman Institute for a lecture by &lt;strong&gt;Marika Kuzma&lt;/strong&gt;. Moderated by &lt;a href="https://harriman.columbia.edu/person/mark-andryczyk/"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mark Andryczyk&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In anticipation of her concert at the Cathedral of St. John the Divine on January 9th, Dr. Marika Kuzma, professor emerita of UC Berkeley and artistic director of the professional chamber choir Ensemble Cherubim, will discuss the brilliant phenomenon of a cappella music in Ukraine: how it has intersected with Ukraine&amp;#39;s political history and how its little-known treasures are unique within international choral repertoire. Each piece she will present&amp;mdash;from carols to sacred concertos to choral fantasies by current composers&amp;mdash;carries a unique, powerful story.&lt;/p&gt;

