&lt;p&gt;Content creators have evolved from social media personalities into media businesses, entrepreneurs, storytellers, and powerful brand partners. At the same time, the platforms that connect creators, brands, and audiences are changing rapidly as algorithms, AI-powered discovery, virtual creators, and AI agents increasingly shape what people see, trust, buy, and share.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This panel will bring together leaders from the creator, brand, platform, and technology ecosystem to explore how influence is changing and what that means for the future of communication and marketing. They&amp;rsquo;ll examine how content creators are building businesses and communities, how brands are rethinking creator partnerships, how major platforms are shaping discovery and engagement, and how AI is becoming a more active participant on both sides of the marketplace.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The panel will also explore questions around authenticity, trust, creativity, ownership, audience discovery, and the evolving relationship among creators, brands, platforms, and consumers.&lt;/p&gt;
