&lt;p&gt;The Offices of Inclusive Excellence and Education&amp;nbsp;are pleased to invite the Columbia&amp;nbsp;Community to&amp;nbsp;the &lt;strong&gt;Undesign the Redline&amp;nbsp;Exhibit Discussion&lt;/strong&gt; on Wednesday, November 18, 5-6:30pm in the Riverview Lounge, Allan Rosenfield Building.&amp;nbsp;&lt;em&gt;&lt;a href="https://nam02.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fus.list-manage.com%2FS8LrFxwzl3g%3Fe%3D23fa5f2f14%26c2id%3De7a9522cd9b644eff00fe9d62183ac74&amp;amp;data=05%7C02%7Cdj2670%40cumc.columbia.edu%7Ca3546640ab184022dfe108df2ad1d904%7Cb0002a9b0017404d97dc3d3bab09be81%7C0%7C0%7C639276752946140032%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&amp;amp;sdata=9gqfNh2R%2B00pcSL3A%2FaVtM9RyEzRTtjJ6GX%2B6X4%2BiAE%3D&amp;amp;reserved=0" target="_blank"&gt;Undesign the Redline&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;/em&gt;an interactive exhibit by Designing the We,&amp;nbsp;explores the design of policies like redlining, their implications for today, and what we can do to &amp;ldquo;undesign&amp;rdquo; them. We will be joined in discussion by Braden Crooks, Co-Founder of Designing the We.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Questions raised by the&amp;nbsp;exhibit include:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Space: How have policies, institutions, infrastructure, and resource allocation physically organized opportunity and disadvantage?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Place: How does a neighborhood&amp;#39;s history continue to affect the health of people living there?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
