&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;quot;Toward Scalable and Generalizable AI for Medical Image Analysis: From Federated Learning to Probabilistic Representation Learning&amp;quot;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Yading Yuan, PhD, DABR&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
Herbert and Florence Associate Professor of Radiation Oncology (Physics) (in the Data Science Institute)&lt;br /&gt;
Vagelos College of Physicians and Surgeons&lt;br /&gt;
Columbia University Irving Medical Center&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Medical imaging AI is moving toward models that can learn across institutions while adapting to diverse patient populations and imaging conditions. This seminar explores approaches to building scalable and robust AI, from personalized federated learning for collaborative model development without sharing patient data, to probabilistic representation learning that improves generalizability and reduces dependence on manual annotations.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;This research seminar is hosted by the Center for Innovation in Imaging Biomarkers and Integrated Diagnostics (CIMBID) and the Data Science Institute (DSI).&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
